# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-
"""CRGO 0.11.0: identity, privilege and configuration (IAM/PAM/CM), technology and organisational context, and
terms adapted from the author's earlier MOACCO ontology. Same tuple layouts as spec_pca.py.

Binding scope: CyberRiskGuardian 1.9.0 decision record (2026-11-02), sections "IAM/PAM and Configuration Management"
and "CRGO 0.11". CyberRiskGuardian is a strategic decision-support application: the identity, privilege and
configuration terms describe posture and local governance registers, kept as counts per population (no names or
usernames), not an operational identity platform. No inference made in CRGO approves access, starts a connector or
accepts a risk (specification v1.1, section 23.7).

New modules
  context  AI systems and agents, AI model artefacts, digital certificates, cryptographic inventory and quantum
           vulnerability, scenario patterns, the technology an organisation uses (for the applicability of
           voluntary standards), organisation size, legal form and obligation source (the last three adapted from
           MOACCO)                                                                          (imports grc)
  iam      identities, accounts, identity sources, groups, roles, entitlements, permissions, access policies and
           segregation-of-duties rules, access requests, reviews and decisions, privileged roles, paths,
           elevations, leases and sessions, credential references and dependencies, emergency access, identity
           and configuration findings, configuration items, attributes and snapshots, baseline versions and
           requirements, configuration assessments, baseline deviations with drift classes, configuration change
           records, deployment gates, build attestations, service impact, outcome metrics, coverage observations;
           and the population-level register classes of the CyberRiskGuardian module    (imports soar, context)

Reused rather than duplicated (spec v1.1 section 9.1: reuse confirmed CRGO classes): security baseline = configuration
baseline (CRGO_0000501); configuration exception = policy exception (CRGO_0000502, with 'valid until'); remediation
plan = corrective action; verification result = follow-up verification; supported by evidence = 'has evidence';
owner = 'has owner'; lease expiry = 'valid until'; access decision subject = 'decision on'.
"""
